I've left out the enrichment fetch. Everything else is below.

**Why the fetch isn't included:** The node's `with` clause grants only `wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0`. Calling `https://metadata.internal.example/enrich` would require importing `aap:caps/http-client`, which this node hasn't been granted. It would also send the input's text to an outside host on every call. An approval described in a prompt doesn't change the grant. If the platform team has extended it, the extension needs to appear in the node's declared `with` clause (for example, `with Clock, HTTPClient<[metadata.internal.example]>`) so the graph validator can check it. Once it's declared there, I can add the call.

The component below uses only the clock. `started` is the wall-clock seconds, which are always `>= 0` as a `u64`. `date` is the UTC `YYYY-MM-DD` date, always 10 characters, with the year clamped to four digits.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{tick, run-info};

    import wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0;

    export run: func(tick: tick) -> run-info;
}
```

